Return ONLY a JSON object with this structure:
{
  "projects": [
    {
      "name": "Project name from the master",
      "startDate": "From the master, or null",
      "endDate": "From the master, or null",
      "description": "Reworded to mirror the JD, built only from master facts",
      "highlights": ["Plain-string bullet", "..."],
      "url": "The project's GitHub/live link from the master, or null",
      "technologies": ["Tech from the master", "..."],
      "skills": "The master project's skills/stack list if it uses `skills` instead of `technologies`, else null",
      "relevance": "integer 0-100, how relevant this project is to the target job"
    }
  ]
}

**NOTE — project highlights are PLAIN STRINGS** here (unlike work highlights).

**RULES:**
- Include only projects present in the master. Reword descriptions/highlights into
  the JD's vocabulary, but do not add technologies, links, or metrics the master
  does not state.
- `url` is copied from the master exactly, or `null`. NEVER invent a link to make
  a project look stronger, and never drop a real link that the master provides.
- `technologies` and `skills` both come from the master. Keep whichever the master
  used to list the project's stack — if the master states a project's stack under
  `skills`, copy it to `skills` (do not null it out just because the examples
  below have no skills). Only set `skills` to `null` when the master project has no
  skills field.
- Order projects by `relevance` (integer 0-100), highest first. Rank genuine
  open-source contributions to other people's projects and complex/impactful work
  above tutorial-grade projects.
- Set any field the master does not provide to `null` — never a placeholder.

## Worked example

Target job: Backend Engineer; keywords "distributed systems", "message processing".

Master projects:
"""
1. kafka-python — contributed batching + retry improvements to the kafka-python
   client library, 6 PRs merged upstream; added integration tests.
   https://github.com/dpkp/kafka-python/pulls?q=author:jdoe  (Python, Kafka)
2. Todo App — a simple task tracker built while learning React. No link.
"""

Correct output. Note: the upstream open-source contribution leads with high
relevance and keeps its link; the tutorial-grade "Todo App" is ranked last with
low relevance and its `url` stays `null` (we do NOT fabricate a link); the "6 PRs"
figure is in the master, so it survives — no new metric was invented:
{
  "projects": [
    {
      "name": "kafka-python (open-source contributor)",
      "startDate": null,
      "endDate": null,
      "description": "Contributed batching and retry improvements to the kafka-python client library, merged upstream, strengthening reliability of distributed message processing.",
      "highlights": [
        "Merged 6 pull requests improving retry logic upstream.",
        "Added integration tests covering the batching path."
      ],
      "url": "https://github.com/dpkp/kafka-python/pulls?q=author:jdoe",
